From: Sonar platform maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ports/linux: define SYS_openat2 with older host headers

Keep the openat2 syscall intercept enabled when pseudo is built with older
Linux headers, including when its native sstate is reused on another host.
Adapted to the EDF 25.05 pseudo source from the two upstream changes below.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.yoctoproject.org/pseudo/commit/?id=899736ef46bb903099e13d649cfe785c29135cab]
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.yoctoproject.org/pseudo/commit/?id=43cbd8fb4914328094ccdb4bb827d74b1bac2046]

--- a/ports/linux/portdefs.h
+++ b/ports/linux/portdefs.h
@@ -53,3 +53,12 @@
 #define _MKNOD_VER 1
 #endif
 #endif
+
+/* Ubuntu 20.04, Debian 11 and Opensuse 15.5 need this */
+#ifndef SYS_openat2
+/* openat2 has syscall number 437 on the supported Linux architectures. */
+#ifndef __NR_openat2
+#define __NR_openat2 437
+#endif
+#define SYS_openat2 __NR_openat2
+#endif
